F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:3:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:4:Step 1: the reconstruction is a strict subset of the original (0 extra pairs);
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:5:        all missing pairs' A-side ids are absent from the matcher's input.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:6:Step 2: all 1,615 of those A-side records ARE in clean_names_1930_old, are male,
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:7:        and have bpl and race -- but 791 have a blank FIRST name and 947 a blank
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:8:        LAST name. run_full_census_prep.do drops them because a record with no
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:9:        initial cannot be blocked.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:10:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:11:ABE matches on EXACT cleaned names. So if a pair's 1930 first name is blank, its
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:12:1940 first name must be blank too, or they could not have matched. This script
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:13:checks that directly in the original link file rather than inferring it, and
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:14:reports what fraction of the missing pairs are joined on an empty name field.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:15:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:16:That decides how to read the shortfall: if these are blank-on-blank joins, the
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:17:reconstruction is not missing real links -- it is declining to make spurious
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:18:ones, and is arguably the better output.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:19:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall_step3.do:20:Reads only.
