F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:1:/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:2:Why does the full-count ABE reconstruction fall ~1,600 pairs short?
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:3:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:4:run_abe_match.do reproduced Massachusetts EXACTLY (488,439 pairs, identical
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:5:fields). On the full count it lands 1,615 pairs short for the old vintage and
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:6:1,021 short for the new -- 0.0095% and 0.0056%. Small, but Massachusetts was
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:7:exact, so this is not general noise and should be explained rather than
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:8:tolerated.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:9:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:10:The first question is directional:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:11:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:12:  * If the reconstruction is a strict SUBSET of the original, the rule is the
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:13:    same and something is dropping a few pairs at a boundary.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:14:  * If it also contains pairs the original lacks, the two runs are resolving
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:15:    something differently -- ties, ordering, or a parameter that only bites on
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:16:    birthplaces Massachusetts does not exercise.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:17:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:18:Those imply very different fixes, so establish which before theorising.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:19:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:20:Then locate the missing pairs by birthplace. Concentrated in a few birthplaces
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:21:points at a specific failure; spread thinly across many points at tie-breaking.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:22:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:23:Reads only. Writes nothing except a small summary file.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:24:------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:25:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:26:drop _all
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:27:clear all
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:28:set more off
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:29:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:30:if "$ROOT" == "" global ROOT "F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:31:do "$ROOT/code/shared/paths.do"
