F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:50:        di as error "missing: `f'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:51:        exit 601
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:52:    }
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:53:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:54:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:55:di as text _n "{hline 78}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:56:di as result "ABE shortfall diagnosis  --  vintage `vintage'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:57:di as text "{hline 78}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:58:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:59:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:60:* 1. Direction: subset, superset, or both?
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:61:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:62:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:63:use id_A id_B using "`original'", clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:64:quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:65:local n_orig = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:66:tempfile orig
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:67:quietly save `orig'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:68:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:69:use id_A id_B using "`recon'", clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:70:quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:71:local n_recon = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:72:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:73:quietly merge 1:1 id_A id_B using `orig', generate(_m)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:74:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:75:quietly count if _m == 3
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:76:local n_both = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:77:quietly count if _m == 1
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:78:local n_only_recon = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:79:quietly count if _m == 2
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:80:local n_only_orig = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:81:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:82:di as text _n "{hline 78}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:83:di as result "DIRECTION"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:84:di as text "{hline 78}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:85:di as text "  original pairs        : " %14.0fc `n_orig'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:86:di as text "  reconstruction pairs  : " %14.0fc `n_recon'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:87:di as text "  in both               : " %14.0fc `n_both'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:88:di as text "  reconstruction ONLY   : " %14.0fc `n_only_recon'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:89:di as text "  original ONLY         : " %14.0fc `n_only_orig'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:90:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:91:if `n_only_recon' == 0 {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:92:    di as result _n "  => the reconstruction is a strict SUBSET of the original."
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:93:    di as text    "     Same rule; a few pairs are being dropped somewhere."
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:94:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:95:else {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:96:    di as error _n "  => NOT a subset: the reconstruction contains " ///
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:97:       %12.0fc `n_only_recon' " pairs the original lacks."
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:98:    di as text    "     The two runs resolve something differently."
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:99:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:100:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:101:* keep the disagreeing pairs for step 2
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:102:quietly keep if _m != 3
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:103:rename _m _side
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:104:tempfile diff
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:105:quietly save `diff'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:106:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:107:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:108:* 2. Where are they? Build histid -> bpl from the matcher's own inputs.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:109:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:110:* The link files carry no bpl column, so recover it from the per-birthplace
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:111:* input files -- which is exactly the partition the matcher used.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:112:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:113:use "`bpldir'/bpl_list.dta", clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:114:quietly levelsof bpl, local(bpls) clean
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:115:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:116:tempfile map
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:117:local first 1
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:118:foreach b of local bpls {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:119:    quietly use histid using "`bpldir'/bpl_`b'/clean_names_1930.dta", clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:120:    quietly generate int bpl = `b'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:121:    if `first' {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:122:        quietly save `map', replace
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:123:        local first 0
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:124:    }
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:125:    else {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:126:        quietly append using `map'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:127:        quietly save `map', replace
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:128:    }
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:129:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:130:quietly use `map', clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:131:quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:132:local n_map = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:133:quietly duplicates drop histid, force
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:134:quietly save `map', replace
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:135:di as text _n "  A-side id -> bpl map: " %14.0fc `n_map' " ids"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:136:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:137:use `diff', clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:138:rename id_A histid
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:139:quietly merge m:1 histid using `map', keep(1 3) nogenerate
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:140:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:141:di as text _n "{hline 78}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:142:di as result "MISSING PAIRS BY BIRTHPLACE (original only)"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:143:di as text "{hline 78}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:144:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:145:preserve
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:146:    quietly keep if _side == 2
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:147:    quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:148:    local n_miss = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:149:    quietly count if missing(bpl)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:150:    local n_nobpl = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:151:    di as text "  missing pairs         : " %14.0fc `n_miss'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:152:    di as text "  whose A-side id is NOT in any bpl input file : " %10.0fc `n_nobpl'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:153:    if `n_nobpl' > 0 {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:154:        di as error "  ^ those A-side records are absent from the matcher's input"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:155:        di as error "    entirely, so no parameter change could recover them."
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:156:    }
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:157:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:158:    quietly drop if missing(bpl)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:159:    if _N > 0 {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:160:        contract bpl, freq(n_missing)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:161:        gsort -n_missing
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:162:        di as text _n "  top birthplaces by missing pairs:"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:163:        list bpl n_missing in 1/`=min(20,_N)', noobs clean
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:164:        quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:165:        di as text _n "  birthplaces affected : " %6.0f r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:166:    }
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:167:restore
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:168:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:169:di as text _n "{hline 78}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:170:di as result "DONE"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/diagnose_abe_shortfall.do:171:di as text "{hline 78}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:1:/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:2:Validate the ABE reconstruction against the original link files.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:3:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:4:run_abe_match.do is a RECONSTRUCTION: the script that produced
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:5:data/links/link1930_1940_*_noraceblock0.dta does not exist on any drive, and its
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:6:parameters were inferred from the surviving artifacts. Matching row COUNTS would
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:7:be weak evidence -- two different parameterisations can land on similar totals.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:8:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:9:This script asks the decisive question instead: are the pairs the SAME pairs?
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:10:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:11:Method
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:12:------
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:13:The originals are full-census, with no bpl column, so they cannot be filtered to
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:14:Massachusetts directly. But bpl is a blocking variable: every link's A-side
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:15:record lives in exactly one bpl file. So restricting the originals to A-side ids
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:16:that appear in by_bpl/bpl_25 recovers precisely the original's Massachusetts
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:17:links, and that is a like-for-like comparison set for the test run.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:18:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:19:Reports
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:20:-------
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:21:  1. pair-level set agreement (in both / mine only / original only)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:22:  2. for pairs in both: whether every non-key variable agrees
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:23:  3. whether f_name_A holds CLEANED or RAW names -- the one remaining ambiguity
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:24:     in the reconstruction, since both are str16 and width cannot discriminate
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:25:------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:26:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:27:drop _all
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:28:clear all
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:29:set more off
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:30:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:31:if "$ROOT" == "" global ROOT "F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:32:do "$ROOT/code/shared/paths.do"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:33:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:34:local vintage "old"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:35:local test_bpl 25
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:36:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:37:if "`vintage'" == "old" {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:38:    local bpldir "$ABEJW/data/by_bpl"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:39:    local tag    "ans_cleaned"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:40:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:41:else {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:42:    local bpldir "$ABEJW/data/by_bpl_new_transcription"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:43:    local tag    "true_cleaned"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:44:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:45:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:46:local original    "$D_LINKS/link1930_1940_`tag'_noraceblock0.dta"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:47:local reconstruct "$ABEJW/data/matched_abe_`vintage'/link1930_1940_`tag'_noraceblock0_bpl`test_bpl'.dta"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:48:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:49:foreach f in "`original'" "`reconstruct'" {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:50:    capture confirm file "`f'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:51:    if _rc {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:52:        di as error "missing: `f'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:53:        exit 601
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:54:    }
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:55:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:56:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:57:di as text _n "{hline 74}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:58:di as result "Validating ABE reconstruction  --  vintage `vintage', bpl `test_bpl'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:59:di as text "{hline 74}"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:60:di as text "  original    : `original'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:61:di as text "  reconstruct : `reconstruct'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:62:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:63:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:64:* 1. A-side universe for this bpl
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:65:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:66:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:67:use histid using "`bpldir'/bpl_`test_bpl'/clean_names_1930.dta", clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:68:rename histid id_A
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:69:quietly duplicates drop id_A, force
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:70:quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:71:local n_univ = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:72:tempfile univ
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:73:quietly save `univ'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:74:di as text _n "  A-side ids in bpl `test_bpl' : " %12.0fc `n_univ'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:75:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:76:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:77:* 2. Restrict the originals to that universe
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:78:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:79:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:80:use "`original'", clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:81:quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:82:local n_orig_all = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:83:quietly merge m:1 id_A using `univ', keep(3) nogenerate
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:84:quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:85:local n_orig_bpl = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:86:di as text "  original links, all bpl      : " %12.0fc `n_orig_all'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:87:di as text "  original links, bpl `test_bpl' only  : " %12.0fc `n_orig_bpl'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:88:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:89:* rename so the merge below can compare rather than silently keep master values
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:90:foreach v of varlist _all {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:91:    if !inlist("`v'", "id_A", "id_B") rename `v' o_`v'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:92:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:93:tempfile orig
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:94:quietly save `orig'
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:95:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:96:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:97:* 3. Pair-level set comparison
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:98:*==============================================================================
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:99:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:100:use "`reconstruct'", clear
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:101:quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:102:local n_recon = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:103:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:104:* Is (id_A,id_B) actually a key? abematch iterates age bands, so in principle a
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:105:* pair could be emitted more than once. Check before merging rather than letting
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:106:* a 1:1 merge abort the run.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:107:quietly duplicates tag id_A id_B, generate(_dup)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:108:quietly count if _dup > 0
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:109:local n_dup_recon = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:110:drop _dup
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:111:if `n_dup_recon' > 0 {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:112:    di as error _n "  WARNING: " %12.0fc `n_dup_recon' ///
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:113:       " reconstruction rows share an (id_A,id_B) pair"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:114:    di as error "  deduplicating before the comparison"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:115:    quietly duplicates drop id_A id_B, force
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:116:    quietly count
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:117:    di as error "  rows after dedup: " %12.0fc r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:118:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:119:else di as text _n "  (id_A,id_B) is unique in the reconstruction"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:120:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:121:capture merge 1:1 id_A id_B using `orig', generate(_cmp)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:122:if _rc {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:123:    di as error "  merge 1:1 failed (rc = " _rc ")"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:124:    di as error "  (id_A,id_B) is not unique in the ORIGINAL -- rerun with m:1"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:125:    exit _rc
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:126:}
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:127:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:128:quietly count if _cmp == 3
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:129:local n_both = r(N)
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/01_abe_jw/linkage/validate_abe_reconstruction.do:130:quietly count if _cmp == 1
