F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:1:/*------------------------------------------------------------------------------
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:2:verify_paths.do -- check that every path this package depends on resolves.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:3:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:4:Run this after moving the package, changing ROOT, or reorganising data. It
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:5:touches nothing and takes seconds. Every global in paths.do is checked, then
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:6:the specific files each pipeline needs.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:7:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:8:    Start-Process "C:\Program Files (x86)\Stata15\StataMP-64.exe" `
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:9:      -ArgumentList '/e','do','"F:\Deaglan\Census_Transcriptions\code\shared\verify_paths.do"' `
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:10:      -Wait -NoNewWindow -WorkingDirectory "F:\Deaglan\Census_Transcriptions\output\logs"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:11:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:12:Exits 0 if everything resolves, 9 if anything is missing.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:13:------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:14:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:15:drop _all
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:16:clear all
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:17:set more off
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:18:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:19:if "$ROOT" == "" global ROOT "F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:20:do "$ROOT/code/shared/paths.do"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:21:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:22:global NFAIL 0
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:23:
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:24:* Check one file. This is a program rather than a loop over a list because
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:25:*     local files "A" "B" "C"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:26:* does NOT create a three-element list: Stata strips only the outermost quote
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:27:* pair, so the macro becomes  A" "B" "C  and the first element carries a stray
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:28:* trailing quote. That silently reports a present file as missing.
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:29:capture program drop chkfile
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:30:program define chkfile
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:31:    args f
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:32:    capture confirm file "`f'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:33:    if _rc {
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:34:        di as error "  MISS  `f'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:35:        global NFAIL = $NFAIL + 1
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:36:    }
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:37:    else di as result "  OK    " as text "`f'"
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:38:end
F:/Deaglan/Census_Transcriptions/code/shared/verify_paths.do:39:
